From 4eb15ad53af653df5f5df91039b2847d24c9b944 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan <nsafran1217@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:54:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] sn2: drain the old CPU's PIO writes when a task migrates

SN2 doesn't order PIO writes issued from different CPUs.  sn_setup()
sets IA64_THREAD_MIGRATION on the boot task, which every task inherits,
and until 5.4 switch_to() then called platform_migrate() = sn_migrate()
whenever a task resumed on a CPU other than the one it last ran on.
sn_migrate() waits for the previous CPU's SHub to drain its PIO writes,
so a thread with MMIO mapped (a user-space driver, mspec, a DRM BO in
VRAM) can't have its writes overtaken by writes from its new CPU.

The machvec removal dropped the call but left the IA64_THREAD_MIGRATION
test and the last_cpu update, and the SN2 restore didn't put the call
back, so sn_migrate() has had no caller.  Restore it.  On a non-SN2
kernel nothing sets IA64_THREAD_MIGRATION and the hook is empty.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 arch/ia64/include/asm/switch_to.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/ia64/include/asm/switch_to.h b/arch/ia64/include/asm/switch_to.h
index 1202b3160dac..3b5369630df4 100644
--- a/arch/ia64/include/asm/switch_to.h
+++ b/arch/ia64/include/asm/switch_to.h
@@ -53,6 +53,13 @@ extern void ia64_load_extra (struct task_struct *task);
 } while (0)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SMP
+#ifdef CONFIG_IA64_SGI_SN2
+extern void sn_migrate(struct task_struct *task);
+#define ia64_platform_migrate(task)	sn_migrate(task)
+#else
+#define ia64_platform_migrate(task)	do { } while (0)
+#endif
+
 /*
  * In the SMP case, we save the fph state when context-switching away from a thread that
  * modified fph.  This way, when the thread gets scheduled on another CPU, the CPU can
@@ -70,6 +77,7 @@ extern void ia64_load_extra (struct task_struct *task);
 	if (unlikely((current->thread.flags & IA64_THREAD_MIGRATION) &&	       \
 		     (task_cpu(current) !=				       \
 		      		      task_thread_info(current)->last_cpu))) { \
+		ia64_platform_migrate(current);				       \
 		task_thread_info(current)->last_cpu = task_cpu(current);       \
 	}								       \
 } while (0)
